# WM8960 Audio Driver HAT ctrl list (X5): one amixer cset name= per line.
# Control names verified against kernel/sound/soc/codecs/wm8960.c
# wm8960_snd_controls[]; initial values copied from the in-tree x3
# alsactl baseline (debian/etc/hobot_audio_config/x3/wm8960_config/
# wm8960_asound.state). gain baseline: driver default, hw-verify pending.
# Acceptance correction 2026-11-19 (main session review): dropped
# 'Left/Right Boost Mixer LINPUT1 Switch' - the driver only declares the
# LINPUT1 Volume controls, no per-input Switch.
# Syntax note: cset name= is used uniformly across ALL .ctrl assets
# (spec x5_audio_profile_migration_spec.md section on the es8156 sset
# blind spot); for wm8960 both forms resolve, cset keeps one convention.
amixer -c0 cset name='Capture Switch' on,on
amixer -c0 cset name='Capture Volume' 39,39
amixer -c0 cset name='ADC PCM Capture Volume' 195,195
amixer -c0 cset name='ADC High Pass Filter Switch' off
amixer -c0 cset name='Left Input Boost Mixer LINPUT1 Volume' 3
amixer -c0 cset name='Right Input Boost Mixer RINPUT1 Volume' 3
amixer -c0 cset name='Playback Volume' 255,255
amixer -c0 cset name='Headphone Playback Volume' 109,109
amixer -c0 cset name='Speaker Playback Volume' 109,109
amixer -c0 cset name='ALC Function' Off
